{"name":"Andorra","hex":"#633737","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Andorra","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A microstate in Southern Europe, between Spain and France. Official name: Principality of Andorra. Capital and largest city: Andorra la Vella. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Andorra"}],"entries":[{"title":"Andorra","blocks":[{"text":"Andorra, officially the Principality of Andorra, is a landlocked country on the Iberian Peninsula, in the eastern Pyrenees in southwestern Europe, bordered by France to the north and Spain to the south. Believed to have been created by Charlemagne, Andorra was ruled by the count of Urgell until 988, when it was transferred to the Diocese of Urgell. Andorra was formed as a polity by a charter in 1278, being a lordship within the Principality of Catalonia until 1715. It is currently headed by two co-princes: the Bishop of Urgell in Catalonia, Spain, and the president of France. Its capital and largest city is Andorra la Vella."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Flag_of_Andorra.svg/330px-Flag_of_Andorra.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andorra"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Gravats_del_Roc_de_les_Bruixes.JPG/500px-Gravats_del_Roc_de_les_Bruixes.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Gravats_del_Roc_de_les_Bruixes.JPG/1280px-Gravats_del_Roc_de_les_Bruixes.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Gravats_del_Roc_de_les_Bruixes.JPG/500px-Gravats_del_Roc_de_les_Bruixes.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Roc de les Bruixes prehistorical sanctuary in Canillo (detail)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGravats_del_Roc_de_les_Bruixes.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Ann%C3%ADbal%2C_andosins.png/500px-Ann%C3%ADbal%2C_andosins.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Ann%C3%ADbal%2C_andosins.png/500px-Ann%C3%ADbal%2C_andosins.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hannibal's route (red) during the Second Punic War. The Iberian tribes (green) fought against the Carthaginian army in the Pyrenees.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnn%C3%ADbal%2C_andosins.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Charlemagne_et_Louis_le_Pieux.jpg/500px-Charlemagne_et_Louis_le_Pieux.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Charlemagne_et_Louis_le_Pieux.jpg/1280px-Charlemagne_et_Louis_le_Pieux.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Charlemagne_et_Louis_le_Pieux.jpg/500px-Charlemagne_et_Louis_le_Pieux.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Charlemagne instructing his son, Louis the Pious","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACharlemagne_et_Louis_le_Pieux.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Parr%C3%B2quies_andorra.png/500px-Parr%C3%B2quies_andorra.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Parr%C3%B2quies_andorra.png/500px-Parr%C3%B2quies_andorra.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The six old parishes, each named for their patron saint, as depicted in the Acta de Consagració i Dotació de la Catedral de la Seu d'Urgell (839)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AParr%C3%B2quies_andorra.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Esgl%C3%A9sia_de_Sant_Joan_de_Caselles_-_7.jpg/500px-Esgl%C3%A9sia_de_Sant_Joan_de_Caselles_-_7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Esgl%C3%A9sia_de_Sant_Joan_de_Caselles_-_7.jpg/1280px-Esgl%C3%A9sia_de_Sant_Joan_de_Caselles_-_7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Esgl%C3%A9sia_de_Sant_Joan_de_Caselles_-_7.jpg/500px-Esgl%C3%A9sia_de_Sant_Joan_de_Caselles_-_7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sant Joan de Caselles church, dating from the 11th century, part of the Andorran Romanesque heritage","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEsgl%C3%A9sia_de_Sant_Joan_de_Caselles_-_7.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/065_Absis_de_Sant_Miquel_d%27Engolasters.jpg/500px-065_Absis_de_Sant_Miquel_d%27Engolasters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/065_Absis_de_Sant_Miquel_d%27Engolasters.jpg/1280px-065_Absis_de_Sant_Miquel_d%27Engolasters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/065_Absis_de_Sant_Miquel_d%27Engolasters.jpg/500px-065_Absis_de_Sant_Miquel_d%27Engolasters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Apse fresco of Sant Miquel d'Engolasters church, painted by Mestre de Santa Coloma during the 12th century[48]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A065_Absis_de_Sant_Miquel_d'Engolasters.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w